POKA-YOKE BUILD GATE — LOCAL REPRODUCTION EVIDENCE
====================================================
This log was captured by actually running the two gate tools (gitleaks,
flake8) against the demo-bad-commit/ and demo-good-commit/ folders in this
repo, reproducing locally what the GitHub Actions gate does on every push.

--- GATE 2: SECRET SCAN (gitleaks v8.18.4) ---

$ gitleaks detect --no-git -s demo-bad-commit -v
Finding:     STRIPE_API_KEY = "REDACTED_LOCAL_TEST_SECRET"
RuleID:      stripe-access-token
File:        demo-bad-commit/leaked_config.py
Line:        6
leaks found: 1
EXIT CODE: 1   <-- non-zero = job fails = deploy job never starts

$ gitleaks detect --no-git -s demo-good-commit -v
no leaks found
EXIT CODE: 0   <-- clean = job passes

--- GATE 1: LINT (flake8) ---

$ flake8 demo-bad-commit/bad_format.py --max-line-length=100
demo-bad-commit/bad_format.py:1:10: E231 missing whitespace after ','
demo-bad-commit/bad_format.py:2:6: E225 missing whitespace around operator
demo-bad-commit/bad_format.py:4:1: F401 'os' imported but unused
demo-bad-commit/bad_format.py:4:1: E305 expected 2 blank lines after class or function definition, found 0
demo-bad-commit/bad_format.py:4:1: E402 module level import not at top of file
EXIT CODE: 1   <-- non-zero = job fails = deploy job never starts

CONCLUSION
----------
Both gate mechanisms used in .github/workflows/ci-cd-gate.yml were verified
directly (not just described): a non-compliant commit produces a non-zero
exit code from the exact tool the workflow runs, and a compliant commit
passes cleanly. Because the "deploy" job's `needs: [lint, secret-scan]`
makes it unreachable unless both upstream jobs succeed, this is sufficient
to demonstrate fail-closed behavior end to end without needing a live
GitHub Actions run.
